{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"clippable-holy-gourami","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Bounded completion recovery is unreachable for a step-budget exhaustion\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a].\n\n`CompletionAgentStep.run` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:426-432`) catches ONLY\n`UnretryableOutputError`, and only when `_is_token_exhaustion(exc)` holds. A step-budget exhaustion\nraises `LLMRunnerError` (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:95-103`), and per\n`src/rebar/llm/errors.py:29-46` `LLMRunnerError` is a strict ANCESTOR of `UnretryableOutputError`\n— so it never matches and the recovery never engages.\n\nConfirmed by experiment, with a control: a synthetic budget `LLMRunnerError` fed to\n`CompletionAgentStep.run` PROPAGATED and left `failure_diagnostic is None`; the control, an\n`UnretryableOutputError` truncation, ENTERED recovery.\n\nThis matters because bounded recovery is exactly the mechanism the failure needs. It isolates each\nexplicit criterion in a FRESH agentic history (so a loop cannot persist across criteria), withdraws\ntools at 16 run steps, and finishes with a tool-free structured finalizer — see\n`docs/llm-framework.md:720+`. The error message printed to the operator says \"narrow the task\", and\nthis is the machinery that does exactly that, sitting unreachable one `except` clause away.\n\nFor epic e369 it would fit: 14 explicit criteria (<= `_MAX_CRITERIA` 32), context 99,347 chars vs\nthe 100,000 `_MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS` cap — though that is only **653 chars of headroom**, which is its\nown fragility worth sizing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a step-budget exhaustion routes into the bounded per-criterion recovery instead of propagating\n- [ ] the truncation path keeps its current behaviour exactly (regression pinned by a test)\n- [ ] recovery still fails CLOSED when it cannot produce full criterion coverage — this must never\n      become a route to an unearned PASS\n- [ ] a test drives a budget exhaustion end to end and asserts recovery ran and produced a verdict","id":"fd84-92b4-01ba-4911","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bounded completion recovery is unreachable for a step-budget exhaustion (LLMRunnerError is not UnretryableOutputError)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785932595294557001,"uuid":"3942e3e9-1f16-4e21-bd91-942bf5e816d3"}